  "text": "Parliament House,\nCANBERRA.\nA.C.T.\nJune 9th. 1955.\nDear Mr. McFadyen,\nI would like to extend my heartiest\ncongratulations on the honour\nconferred upon jou to-day•\nIt must be very gratifying to feel\nthat\nafter\nall these years, your\nservices have been recognised by\nHer Majesty\nr the Queen•\nYours sincerely,\n(GEORGE MCLEAY)\nSmitten.\nMr. C. H. McFadyen, C.B.E•,\nsecretary:\nDepartment of Shipping & Irans ports\nMELBOURNE•\nC.1.",
